The script sends a `GET` request to the target URL. The server parses the path `/api/v1/v1.0.1/v1.0.1/v1.0.1/v1.0.1/`. Since the full path matches the expected format, the server recognizes the request as a legitimate API call.

Once the request is accepted, the script sends an `OPTIONS` request to `/api/v1/v1.0.1/v1.0.1/v1.0.1/v1.0.1/OPTIONS`. The server responds with a JSON payload containing the HTTP status code (`200` for success), the method (`GET`), and the response headers (headers like `Accept: application/json`).

In the response, you will find the data you need. The JSON object will typically include an `api_data` key or a nested `data` object containing the values you are looking for.

